# RotaryKit, from BrianEnders/pebble-rotary-kit, kept in its upstream formatting.
#
# The original reason was that our copy was byte-identical to upstream apart from two bug fixes,
# so reformatting would have buried them in 300 lines of whitespace and made the patch
# unsendable. That is no longer true: four commits on this fork have rewritten a large part of
# rotary_kit.c -- the gesture geometry, the wheel's acceleration, the hold and swipe handling --
# so it is fork code now, not a vendored copy with a patch on top.
#
# It stays exempt anyway, for a weaker but still real reason: what remains shared with upstream
# is easier to see in a diff which is not also a whitespace diff, and the two bug fixes are still
# worth sending back. Reformatting it is a reasonable thing to decide to do; it should just be
# decided, in a commit of its own which changes nothing else, rather than happening by accident
# on the day someone removes these lines.
